-- Support ideals, the partition torsor and the subordinate partition of
-- unity, Serre note Sections 6-8 (agent J): SerreSupportIdeal,
-- SerrePartitionIndex, SerrePartition, SerreSupportIdealSaturation,
-- SerreSupportIdealLambda, SerrePartitionQuasiCoherent, SerrePartitionCover.
-- Support laws, invertibility opens, slices and charts are used by their
-- named lemmas; the canonical lambda maps, their clearing/killing form,
-- products, chart ring fact and lambda-criterion are agent L's named
-- interfaces. Structural module/sheaf/product/kernel records, small type
-- aliases and the regular module stay open to expose carriers; no
-- quotient, localisation, gluing or sheaf proof construction is reopened.
-- The torsor and the global lift are SerreTorsorLifts' for the sum map.
